Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 03:12:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?feat(budget):=20wire=20window-burn=20metering?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20=E2=80=94=20consumedPoints=20per=20window?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add window-meter.ts, the pure half of the meter budgetGate() has been
waiting on: UsageSample {at, points}, windowStart(), consumedPoints()
(sum of samples inside the budget's CURRENT rolling or calendar window,
future samples ignored), unitsToPoints() (tokens -> points through the
budget's conversion) and meterBudget() (planCapacity with the live-burn
axis filled in). Clock-injected and dependency-free so it is deterministic
under test.

Wire it into budget-check.ts: a new optional --ledger <path> reads a JSON
array of {at, points} / {at, units} samples and meters the window as of
Date.now(); the decision moves into an exported pure evaluate() so it is
testable without Deno.exit. Existing flags, exit codes and the fail-open
posture are unchanged — no ledger (or an unreadable one) still means
consumedPoints=0 with only the static envelope enforced, now logged as a
warning instead of silently.

front-desk-budget.yml gains an optional `ledger` input (passed through
only when non-empty, with a read grant scoped to that one file);
window-meter.ts joins the check task, the jsr-check step, the JSR
exports/publish list, and CLAUDE.md.

Tests: window-meter_test.ts asserts consumedPoints accumulates inside a
rolling window and slides samples out as they age, and accumulates inside
a calendar window and resets to zero at the boundary; budget-check_test.ts
covers the ledger parser and the gate's fail-open / fail-closed paths.

This does NOT close #10. The issue asks for real per-window burn wired
into budget-check.ts and depends on the telemetry/OTLP metering source,
which is not yet filed in this repo. This lands the meter and the
--ledger seam that source will emit into; no caller of
front-desk-budget.yml supplies a ledger today, so production behaviour
is unchanged (unmetered, fail-open) until an emitter exists.

Refs #10, epic #5
Claim-issue: bounded-systems/gh-project-room#10

